Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:05:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(network): finish transport-initiated RakNet disconnects

RakNet emits a disconnect reason before closing its application pipeline.
Treat that event as an already initiated disconnect so the core close handler
does not start another handshake against a session in DISCONNECTING state.

A direct Java 26.3 connection to Bedrock 1.26.51.1 (protocol 2193) stays
active after the peer goes silent: the session detects its 30-second timeout,
but the repeated disconnect never completes. This affects the shared handler
used by direct connections and ViaProxy. Local closes still send one orderly
disconnect, and transport events continue to downstream handlers.

Embedded transport tests cover every RakNet reason and local close completion.
The resolved Cloudburst and VFP runtime session codecs both emit the event
before closing; no runtime-library reflection or client workaround is needed.
